## Firewall

UFW was initially not installed.

Installed it using:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ufw
```

Configured the default incoming policy:

```bash
sudo ufw default deny incoming
```

Configured outgoing traffic:

```bash
sudo ufw default allow outgoing
```

Allowed SSH:

```bash
sudo ufw allow 22/tcp
```

Enabled the firewall:

```bash
sudo ufw enable
```

Verified:

```bash
sudo ufw status verbose
```

Final firewall configuration:

```text
Status: active
Logging: on (low)
Default: deny (incoming)
Default: allow (outgoing)
```

SSH:

```text
22/tcp ALLOW IN Anywhere
22/tcp ALLOW IN Anywhere (v6)
```

## Open Port Verification

After enabling UFW:

```bash
sudo ss -lntup
```

SSH remained available:

```text
0.0.0.0:22
[::]:22
```

This confirmed that enabling the firewall did not interrupt SSH access.

## Service Audit

Audited enabled services:

```bash
systemctl list-unit-files --type=service --state=enabled
```

Audited running services:

```bash
systemctl --type=service --state=running
```

Important services intentionally retained:

```text
ssh.service
NetworkManager.service
wpa_supplicant.service
avahi-daemon.service
kl-sophos.service
klef-auth.service
systemd-timesyncd.service
udisks2.service
```

### Avahi

Avahi was intentionally retained because the Pi is accessed using:

```bash
ssh bhavyesh_bhavvi@bhavyesh.local
```

The `.local` hostname uses mDNS.

Avahi is listening on UDP 5353.

Therefore, disabling Avahi would interfere with the current `.local` hostname workflow.

### KLEF Services

These services were retained because they are part of the current KLEF Wi-Fi and captive-portal automation:

```text
kl-sophos.service
klef-auth.service
```

### Serial Console

Investigated:

```text
serial-getty@ttyAMA10.service
```

The kernel command line contains:

```text
console=ttyAMA10,115200
```

and:

```text
/dev/serial0 -> ttyAMA10
```

The serial console was therefore intentionally retained for possible low-level recovery and debugging.

### Cloud-init

Cloud-init was also retained.

Checked:

```bash
cloud-init status --long
```

Result:

```text
status: done
errors: []
```

There was a recoverable warning regarding:

```text
cc_netplan_nm_patch
```

but cloud-init completed successfully, so it was not disabled.

## Automatic Security Updates

Installed:

```bash
sudo apt install unattended-upgrades
```

Verified:

```bash
apt-config dump | grep -E 'APT::Periodic::(Update-Package-Lists|Unattended-Upgrade)'
```

Configuration:

```text
APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";
APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "1";
```

This means:

```text
Package list updates → daily
Unattended upgrades  → daily
```

Verified:

```bash
cat /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades
```

Security repositories configured in:

```text
/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50unattended-upgrades
```

include Debian and Debian Security repositories.

Verified timers:

```bash
systemctl list-timers --all | grep -E 'apt|unattended'
```

Active timers:

```text
apt-daily.timer
apt-daily-upgrade.timer
```

Automatic reboot was not enabled.

This prevents the Raspberry Pi from unexpectedly rebooting after an update.

## SSH Hardening

Created:

```text
/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-hardening.conf
```

Configuration:

```text
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
```

Validated the configuration:

```bash
sudo sshd -t
```

No errors were returned.

Verified effective settings:

```bash
sudo sshd -T | grep -E '^(permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|pubkeyauthentication|kbdinteractiveauthentication)'
```

Final configuration:

```text
permitrootlogin no
pubkeyauthentication yes
passwordauthentication no
kbdinteractiveauthentication no
```

Reloaded SSH:

```bash
sudo systemctl reload ssh
```

Verified SSH remained active:

```bash
sudo systemctl status ssh --no-pager
```

## SSH Verification

From the Mac, tested:

```bash
ssh bhavyesh_bhavvi@bhavyesh.local
```

The connection succeeded.

This confirmed:

* Avahi/mDNS hostname resolution works
* SSH port 22 remains accessible
* Public-key authentication works
* Password authentication is disabled
* Root SSH login is disabled
* Non-root administration works

